      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "^ This would be better as a option for world creators to add themselves to be honest, there are a bunch of flight sim worlds at the moment that would break if this was made a thing across every instance at a set number.\nI can understand wanting some physics and I do agree that the body jiggle at a certain speed and above is irritating especially in something like the flight sims. However it shouldn't be a across the board non negotiable speed to which you stop gaining speed. It would hold back alot of ideas and creations by world makers. I'm not one myself as I have only made avatars. Just so I'm clear, however if I ever decided to and then my imagination was limited because of an enforced feature I wouldn't be overjoyed to say the least. Not trying to be rude just offering another POV. ^^",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-04-25T05:18:30.743Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Please add terminal velocity to player falling. Jumping off of tall buildings, flying planes, pits, etc, has the player continue to pick up speed indefinitely. Not only is this inaccurate (breaking some Science/Education world ideas I have), but the speed quickly gets so fast that the physics can no longer keep up smoothly, and your body starts wobbling all over when you look at it while falling. A simple limit to 122mph or 53 meters per second, might be good enough, if calculating based on cross-section/mass is too much to ask. Would be good as a toggle for the world possibly as well.",
